# Frozen 2026-09-15, the first run with `--ratchets` on
# (scripts/linux/run-lint-gates.sh, and `ratchets: true` on the CI lane).
# The gate refuses NEW oversized comment blocks and GROWTH in a frozen one; a
# block that shrinks under the limit means DELETING its line here, not editing
# it. Format: <file>	<first line of the block>, which is why no line number
# appears - a block must not re-flag because something above it moved.
#
# Nothing here is a TODO list. Fourteen blocks. Eleven predate the gate and each
# records WHY the code is shaped as it is: which upstream function replaced a
# local fork, which verdict was measured before a strictness switch was removed,
# which failure a guard was written against. The two in
# scripts/linux/lib/antfrastructure.sh are upstream's own template body plus the
# header saying this copy is body-mode - edit the body and the shared-config
# drift gate turns DRIFTED, so the warning has to sit in the file.
#
# The fourteenth came in with origin/develop's cat-stream work (merged
# 2026-09-15): package-producer-bundle.sh's header is the bundle's contract -
# what is exported, what the target host must already have, and the two
# commands you run there - so it sits beside the code for the same reason
# serve.sh's does, one row below.
#
# This repo DOES have a docs/ tree, and moving any of these into it is a real
# option - but it would put the explanation a click away from the twenty lines
# it explains. Do it when a block starts describing a PROCESS rather than the
# code beneath it, not to satisfy a line count.

scripts/agentic-loop/Run-AgenticLoop.sh	# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
scripts/linux/cat-stream/package-producer-bundle.sh	#!/usr/bin/env bash
scripts/linux/cat-stream/serve.sh	#!/usr/bin/env bash
